  "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, angle <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math> is a right angle, point <math alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, and point <math alttext=\"upper Q\"><mi>Q</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> such that <math alttext=\"line segment upper P upper Q\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. If the measure of angle&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper X upper Z upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"63 degree\"><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper P upper Q\"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>?</p>",
