  ],
  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"153\"><mn>153</mn>\n</math>. Since it's given that <math alttext=\"line segment upper P upper Q\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math> is a right angle, angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper Q upper P\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is also a right angle. Angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper P upper Q\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is complementary to angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Z upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math>, which means its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext=\"90 minus 63\"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>. Since angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper P upper Q\"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is supplementary to angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper P upper Q\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext=\"180 minus 27\"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"153\"><mn>153</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
